\ Rung 6: : and ; compile new words from the input.
: SQUARE DUP * ;
7 SQUARE . CR
: CUBE DUP SQUARE * ;
3 CUBE . CR
: SHOUT 72 EMIT 73 EMIT 33 EMIT CR ;
SHOUT
\ An IMMEDIATE word runs while a definition is being compiled: NOW prints
\ its * when LATER is compiled, not when LATER runs.
: NOW 42 EMIT ; IMMEDIATE
: LATER NOW 43 EMIT ;
CR LATER CR
\ : hides the word it defines, so this SQUARE calls the old SQUARE.
: SQUARE SQUARE 1 + ;
4 SQUARE . CR
\ HIDE hides a word by name; FIVE is then unknown.
: FIVE 5 ;
FIVE . HIDE FIVE FIVE CR
\ ' pushes the codeword address (the execution token) of the next word.
: XT-OF-DUP ' DUP ;
5 XT-OF-DUP EXECUTE . . CR
